Accounts Payable Clerk (20 to 32 hours) 20262853 
 - SALARY INDICATION In consultation - JOB GROUP Finance - JOB POSTING NUMBER 720262853 - LOCATION Eindhoven ABOUT THIS JOB OPENING 
Job Description 
You're good at distinguishing between main and secondary financial issues and can handle stress well. You're results-oriented, productive, and excel in a high-pressure environment. You enjoy working both independently and as part of a team. Your colleagues describe you as a hard worker who sets priorities well, is helpful, communicates clearly, and adapts quickly. You take the initiative and are passionate about your work. 
Job Requirements: 
· Process purchase invoices and post expenses based on invoices; 
· Process incoming and outgoing payments; 
· Manage suspense accounts and flag any discrepancies; 
· Serve as the point of contact for financial issues raised by various internal 
stakeholders; 
· You ensure the accurate and timely processing and verification of daily 
bank transactions and payment flows. 
· You provide support to the finance department with various tasks; 
· You assist with financial reviews and the collection of necessary documentation 
for reports and audits. 
· Other related tasks. 
Required skills: 
· MBO+ level (accounting) 
· Accurate, analytical, and meticulous in handling processes 
· You have a good command of Dutch and English (both spoken and 
written); 
· You can work both independently and as part of a team; 
· You are honest and reliable; 
· You are available for 20 to 32 hours per week; 
· Strong communication skills and a sense of responsibility; 
· Strong numerical skills and a solution-oriented mindset; 
· You are a team player and take a problem-solving approach; 
· You are comfortable working with ERP systems (preferably Afas);

32–40 hours per week, in a fixed shift of your choice: morning/afternoon (06:00 – 14:30) or afternoon/evening (14:30 – 22:30).



 Are you ready for a new challenge and would you like to work with high-quality seafood products? For our Operations department in Volendam and/or Edam, we are looking for independent and experienced technical operators to strengthen our team. Does this sound interesting to you? Then keep reading!



 Please note: only candidates who are currently living in the Netherlands can apply.

What will you do?
As an Operator, you will work together with your colleagues in the Operations department to ensure that shrimp production runs safely, productively, and efficiently. Your tasks include:

  - Setting up, converting, adjusting, and operating packaging machines and related equipment;

  - Carrying out various quality and process checks;

  - Cleaning machines according to hygiene and safety regulations;

  - Monitoring product traceability;

  - Contributing to the overall safety and hygiene of our products.

What are we looking for?
As an Operator at Klaas Puul, it is important that you can think in a process-oriented and solution-focused way. You have a proactive attitude and are not afraid to roll up your sleeves. In addition, we expect:

  - A completed technical MBO-level education (preferably VAPRO);

  - Experience in a similar technical role; experience in the food industry is a plus;

  - You must live in the Netherlands; applications from abroad will not be considered;

  - Good teamwork skills, but also the ability to work independently;

  - Good spoken and written English skills; Dutch is a plus;

  - Basic knowledge of food safety and familiarity with guidelines on food fraud and food defense, or the willingness to learn more about these topics.

